RT-07 (P-5 fix 3): fills and copies on the card's own blitter
(build-tree patch against isoriano1968/x11r6.3-amix cb61a21, applied after
zz9000hw-modes.patch, p5-1 .. p5-7 and rt04-monsw-hook.patch).

The Z3660 firmware fills and copies rectangles itself (FILLRECT/COPYRECT),
and the zz9000 driver runs them for a batch of records in one ioctl
(ZZ9KIOC_BLITS, amix-z3660rtg's zz9000.h).  This patch lets the server hand
it the large, simple cases:

  zz9000.h      ZZ9KIOC_BLITS, its records, zz9000BlitMin
  zz9000draw.c  blitFill and copyVRAMBox, the two funnels every window fill
                (SolidRect GXcopy, PaintWindow) and window-to-window copy
                (CopyArea GXcopy, CopyWindow) already goes through, queue a
                record when its area is at least -blitmin pixels and draw it
                on the CPU otherwise; the old bodies are cpuFill/cpuCopy.
                The queue is flushed before any CPU drawing in those paths
                and before each entry point returns, so drawing order is
                kept and nothing else ever sees queued work.  A refusal
                (ENXIO: no blitter on this board or mode; EINVAL: a kernel
                without the ioctl) turns blitting off for the life of the
                server and draws the refused batch on the CPU; the first
                accepted batch logs "card blitter in use".
  amixIo.c      -blitmin N (pixels), in ddxProcessArgument and ddxUseMsg

-blitmin defaults to 0, never: without the option the server draws exactly
as before, so the patch ships inert until the metal A/B picks a value.
Non-GXcopy raster ops and pixmaps stay on the CPU in every case.

